Wings patch 0001: read the encryption key from ODYSSEUS_APP_KEY

Upstream keeps its Fernet keys (data/.app_key for database secrets, data/.key
for api_keys.json) inside the data directory, so every copy of the data
volume, including backups, carries the key that decrypts it. With this patch
both key users take the key from the ODYSSEUS_APP_KEY environment variable
when it is set, and never write a key file in that mode. A malformed key, or
an existing key file that differs from the variable, raises instead of
silently generating a new key and orphaning stored secrets.

Applies to: odysseus-dev/odysseus@9d0d3720f4ca181d87bef94da826d730acc6d483
License: AGPL-3.0-or-later (same as upstream)

